                "end": 8,
                "start": 8
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners argue that many respondents operate abroad through branch offices and can choose to do so without compromising their speech."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioners",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0000-0008"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 12,
                "start": 12
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Petitioners contend that respondents are not subject to the funding condition and therefore cannot assert an unconstitutional\u2011conditions claim, and that foreign entities lack constitutional rights."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Michel",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 23,
                "start": 23
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Michel, petitioners (via Mr. Michel) assert that a U.S. entity that opposes prostitution and sex trafficking can receive funds and use them abroad without needing to work through affiliates."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Michel",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0001-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 27,
                "start": 27
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Michel, petitioners (via Mr. Michel) state that there is no chilling of speech because domestic entities are free to take the money and control their own message."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Michel",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ea1aa2f8b5f1c1178a6f75e529b90eff828a1bbb579b2f264969071016c3286a",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ea1aa2f8b5f1-0001-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 31,
                "start": 31
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Michel, petitioners (via Mr. Michel) emphasize that the program has been a historic success in U.S. foreign aid."
        }
